beginning today the southern nevada  health district will start offering  covet 19 vaccines for kids very young  six months to five years old these will  be pfizer shots because right now  moderna is not available for children  here locally the vaccines recently were  cleared for use on these young children  so you might have some questions about  getting your child vaccinated against  coronavirus well astrid martinez got  some answers from a pediatrician  as the first coveted 19 shots go into  the arms of the youngest americans many  parents have questions about the  vaccines covid vaccination can help with  preventing  severe illness hospitalizations and  deaths in this young age group a common  question why get younger children  vaccinated for covid19 if the illness  can be mild for them dr sarah baslet is  a pediatrician at indiana university  health covett infection is now the  leading infectious cause of death in  children under five and it doesn't seem  like a big deal until it's your child  who's really sick another common  question if my child already had covet  19 do they still need to get the vaccine  they are at risk of getting it again and  the vaccine provides even more  protection over time if your child  currently has covid wait until their  symptoms have gone away and then  schedule their covet vaccine some  parents worry younger children may be  more vulnerable to side effects of the  vaccine but studies show they are  typically mild and can include fever  pain at the injection site fatigue and  irritability as for whether the youngest  kids could suffer the rare side effect  of heart inflammation seen in some  adolescents and adults there were no  cases reported throughout all the  vaccine studies and can children get  their coveted vaccines along with other  regularly scheduled vaccines dr boslitz  says yes astrid martinez cbs news new  york now if your child does experience  side effects after getting the vaccine  then you can give them some  acetaminophen or ibuprofen however  doctors say you shouldn't do that  over-the-counter counter pain reliever  before vaccination only afterwards when  there are symptoms if you're interested  in getting your child vaccinated against  coronavirus you can find a full list of  all the vaccine clinics for children and  adults at eightnewsnow.com
 

